 "version": 1,
 "task": "compose",
 "description": "Put the subject of one photo into another photo. The subject image is scaled to the placement box, matted with BiRefNet (a SUBJECT matter - SAM is a PART segmenter and returns a shirt, not a person), the matte is shrunk 2px before feathering so no backdrop halo survives, and the composite then gets one low-denoise pass so lighting, grain and edges agree. denoise is the whole trick: ~0.22 harmonises, above ~0.35 the face starts dissolving, below ~0.12 the paste stays visible.",
